   "response_text": "Based on my investigation, I've identified an incident:\n\n## Analysis\n\nThe configuration contains an **extreme label noise setting** of `label_noise_fraction: 0.42` (42% of training labels are flipped). This is highly suspicious because:\n\n1. **Unusually high value**: 42% label noise is extreme. Typical noise levels are 0.05-0.15 (5-15%). At 42%, you're flipping nearly half the labels.\n\n2. **Severe impact on learning**: With 42% label noise, the model is trained on severely corrupted labels, which:\n   - Degrades the signal quality immensely\n   - Makes it nearly impossible for the model to learn the true pattern\n   - Results in very slow loss improvement (0.689 \u2192 0.683, only 0.6% reduction over 20 epochs)\n   - Causes validation instability (drops to 0.7578 at epoch 4)\n\n3. **Reasonable default**: Label noise for test/study purposes should typically be in the range 0.05-0.20. A value of 0.42 is outside normal ranges and appears to be a misconfiguration.\n\nThe suspicious configuration line is in `config.resolved.yaml`:\n```yaml\ndata:\n  label_noise_fraction: 0.42\n```\n\nThis should be set to a reasonable value like 0.0 (no noise) or at most 0.15 for robustness studies.",
